    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Eyes of Eirdu.</strong> You and your allies within 10 feet of you have Advantage on saving throws made to avoid or end the Blinded condition.</p><p><strong>Faerie Fire.</strong> You learn the Faerie Fire spell. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it (choose when you take this feat). You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it that way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast it using any spell slots you have. When you cast it without a spell slot through this benefit, taking damage can’t break your Concentration on the spell.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-AwveWwZWi0kaey1o\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Roll the saves against the Blinded condition with Advantage yourself. Skip the Concentration saves of a Faerie Fire cast without a slot.</p></section>",
